"'''Baby Got Back'''" is a song written, co-produced and recorded by American rapper [[Sir Mix-a-Lot]]. Released in May 1992 by [[American Recordings (US)|Def American]] and [[Reprise Records|Reprise]] as the second single from his third album, ''[[Mack Daddy]]'' (1992), the song samples the 1986 [[Detroit techno]] single "Technicolor" by [[Juan Atkins|Channel One]]. At the time of its original release, the song caused controversy because of its outspoken and blatantly sexual lyrics objectifying women, as well as specific references to the [[Cultural history of the buttocks|buttocks]], which some people found objectionable. The song's accompanying music video, directed by [[Adam Bernstein]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thewrap.com/emmy-nominated-directors-strange-trip-from-sir-mix-a-lots-baby-got-back-to-fargo/|title=Emmy Nominated Director's Strange Trip: From Sir-Mix-a-Lot's 'Baby Got Back' to 'Fargo'|last=Pond|first=Steve|work=[[TheWrap]]|date=July 30, 2014|access-date=November 24, 2025}}</ref> was briefly banned by [[MTV]].<ref name="Songfacts">{{cite web |url=http://www.songfacts.com/detail.php?id=604 |title=Baby Got Back by Sir Mix-A-Lot Songfacts  |work=Songfacts |access-date=5 April 2007 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060405141955/http://www.songfacts.com/detail.php?id=604 |archive-date=5 April 2006 |url-status=dead}}</ref> Mix-a-Lot defended the song as being empowering to curvaceous women who were being shown skinny models as an ideal for beauty.

"Baby Got Back" topped the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]], and spent five weeks atop the chart. It was the second best-selling song in the US in 1992<!-- , behind Boyz II Men's "End of the Road" -->. The song was ranked number 17 on [[VH1]]'s "100 Greatest Songs of Hip Hop" in 2008.<ref>{{cite web |last=Winistorfer |first=Andrew |date=2008-09-29 |title=VH1's 100 Greatest Hip-Hop Songs |url=http://www.prefixmag.com/news/vh1s-100-greatest-hip-hop-songs/21901/ |access-date=2011-10-16 |website=Prefixmag.com |archive-date=2014-01-22 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140122235853/http://www.prefixmag.com/news/vh1s-100-greatest-hip-hop-songs/21901/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In October 2023, ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' ranked it among the "500 Best Pop Songs of All Time".<ref name="billboard500bestpopsongs">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/lists/best-pop-songs-all-time-hits/sir-mix-a-lot-baby-got-back/|title=The 500 Best Pop Songs: Staff List|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|date=19 October 2023|access-date=20 October 2023|archive-date=25 November 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231125154633/https://www.billboard.com/lists/best-pop-songs-all-time-hits/sir-mix-a-lot-baby-got-back/|url-status=live}}</ref>

